@startuml agent_collaboration_code
title Ray Agent Collaboration - Code Implementation

skinparam defaultTextAlignment left
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFFCC
skinparam packageBackgroundColor #F5F5F5

' ==================== CODE EXAMPLES ====================
package "Agent Definitions (Ray Actors)" as agents #LightBlue {
    note as agentCode
    <code>
    @ray.remote
    class AgentA:
        def __init__(self):
            self.agent_b = AgentB.remote()  # Reference to Agent B
            self.pending_results = {}

        async def develop_feature(self, task):
            # Working on data download feature
            code = await self.run_claude_code(task)
            
            # Discover need for containerization
            if self.needs_containerization(code):
                # Delegate to Agent B (non-blocking)
                task_ref = ray.put({
                    "code": code,
                    "requirements": ["Dockerfile", "docker-compose"],
                    "callback": self.on_containerization_done
                })
                self.agent_b.do_containerization.remote(task_ref)
            
            # Continue other work while waiting
            return code

        def on_containerization_done(self, result_ref):
            # Callback when Agent B finishes
            result = ray.get(result_ref)
            self.integrate_containerization(result)

    @ray.remote
    class AgentB:
        async def do_containerization(self, task_ref):
            # Get task context
            task = ray.get(task_ref)
            
            # Do the containerization work
            result = await self.run_claude_code(
                f"Containerize this code: {task['code']}"
            )
            
            # Store result and callback
            result_ref = ray.put(result)
            task["callback"](result_ref)  # Notify Agent A
    </code>
    end note
}

' ==================== COMMUNICATION MECHANISM ====================
package "Communication Mechanism" as comm #LightGreen {
    note as commNote
      **Three Ways Agents Collaborate:**

      **1. Shared Object Store (Data)**
      <code>
      # Agent A puts data
      data_ref = ray.put(large_data)
      
      # Agent B gets data (zero-copy if same node)
      data = ray.get(data_ref)
      </code>

      **2. Actor Method Calls (RPC)**
      <code>
      # Agent A calls Agent B's method
      result_ref = agent_b.do_work.remote(data_ref)
      
      # Non-blocking, returns ObjectRef immediately
      # Actual execution happens asynchronously
      </code>

      **3. Callback Pattern (Notification)**
      <code>
      # Agent B notifies Agent A when done
      agent_a.on_complete.remote(result_ref)
      </code>
    end note
}

' ==================== TASK CONTEXT ====================
package "Task Context Structure" as context #LightYellow {
    note as contextNote
      **What Gets Passed Between Agents:**
      <code>
      task_context = {
          # Current state
          "code_snapshot": "...",
          "file_tree": {...},
          "git_branch": "feature/data-download",
          
          # Task requirements
          "task_type": "containerization",
          "requirements": [
              "Create Dockerfile",
              "Add docker-compose.yml",
              "Ensure tests pass in container"
          ],
          
          # Callback for completion
          "callback_actor": agent_a_ref,
          "callback_method": "on_containerization_done",
          
          # Context for Agent B
          "context": {
              "why": "Production deployment needs containerization",
              "constraints": ["Python 3.10+", "FastAPI", "Docker"]
          }
      }
      </code>
    end note
}

' ==================== WORKFLOW ====================
package "Collaboration Workflow" as workflow #LightCoral {
    note as workflowNote
      **Step-by-Step Flow:**

      1. **Agent A** working on feature
         ↓
      2. **Agent A** discovers sub-task needed
         ↓
      3. **Agent A** packages task context
         ↓
      4. **Agent A** calls Agent B (non-blocking)
         ↓
      5. **Agent A** continues other work ← **KEY: Non-blocking**
         ↓
      6. **Agent B** receives task, works on it
         ↓
      7. **Agent B** completes, stores result
         ↓
      8. **Agent B** calls Agent A's callback
         ↓
      9. **Agent A** integrates result
    end note
}

' ==================== KEY INSIGHT ====================
package "Why This Works" as insight #Lavender {
    note as insightNote
      **Key Design Principles:**

      ✓ **Asynchronous** - Agents don't block each other
      ✓ **Stateful** - Each agent maintains its own state (Actor model)
      ✓ **Location Transparent** - Works same whether same/different node
      ✓ **Fault Tolerant** - Ray handles failures, retries
      ✓ **Scalable** - Can have 1000s of agents across cluster

      **vs Simple Message Passing:**
      | Feature | Message Queue | Ray Actors |
      |---------|---------------|------------|
      | State | Stateless | Stateful |
      | Call Pattern | Fire & forget | RPC with return |
      | Data Sharing | Serialize all | Zero-copy refs |
      | Scheduling | Manual | Automatic |
    end note
}

@enduml
